result.conclusion:
CONFIRMED. On live CodinGame, collisions are resolved in the LEGACY entity order. That order is the pre-918c375 `allEntities() = players.flatMap { it.allUnits() } + obstacles`: player 0's creeps (creation order), queen 0, player 1's creeps, queen 1, then the sites. The repo order (all creeps, then both queens, then sites) is not what runs live. Nothing else in the movement code changes. Everything else matches the repo port exactly:
- queens move before the creep phase;
- 5 substeps, each moves every creep by speed/5 and then makes exactly one collisionCheck pass (fixCollisions(all, 1));
- in that pass, each u1 is clamped first and then pushes every overlapping u2 (moving both);
- gaps are 1.0 unit-unit and 1.0 unit-site; masses are queen 10000, knight 400, giant 2000;
- the knight's range test is dist > 50;
- there is no global collision fix at the end of the creep phase or the turn;
- positions are rounded with roundToInt at the end of the turn.

Mechanism: the per-substep pass is order-dependent. Example g892855131 t26. Queen 0 is pushed out of site 6 during her own iteration. Player 1's knight comes after her in the list, so in the same pass it resolves the new overlap and ends at distance 52. In each of the next 4 substeps the knight is out of range (>50), moves in and pushes her ~1.65 → y 457.49 → 457 (replay 457). In the repo order the knight is processed first, so the overlap survives into substep 1. There the knight is at 48.6 < 50 and does not move → 455.87 → 456. The same ordering explains queens ending beyond the clamp (replay x=27..29): enemy knights processed after her clamp push her out. It also explains the given examples g909614601 t31 (now 561,314) and g911493861 t163 (now 60,807).

Two further live rules came out of the plain-turn residue. Both are default in the patch and each has its own switch:
(1) Unit cap (outside movement): TRAIN is refused with "Training too many creeps (N total units requested; 30 maximum)" when the player's creeps plus requested creeps exceed 30. Creeps still in training are not counted, and the warning is also issued for an empty TRAIN. Evidence is the replay's own warning text: 15 occurrences, and 113/113 warning turns now match. Implemented as Const.MAX_UNITS=30; set 999 to disable.
(2) Towers first (spawn-turn HP/order, outside movement): all towers act before the other structures, so newly spawned creeps are never shot on their spawn turn and towers aim at pre-spawn positions. This is the statement order. Rules.TOWERS_FIRST=true; -PtowersFirst=false gives the repo order.
Physics.LEGACY_ENTITY_ORDER=true is the default; -PlegacyOrder=false gives the repo order.
